WEBVTT

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:32.991
Good news, everyone.

00:00:33.075 --> 00:00:38.080
I've invented a device, which allows you
to operate equipment from great distances.

00:00:38.205 --> 00:00:40.916
I call it the Finglonger.

00:00:40.999 --> 00:00:42.482
Observe.

00:00:42.507 --> 00:00:46.021
And... Here we go...

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:48.131
There.

00:00:49.466 --> 00:00:50.717
Pretty long, eh?

00:00:50.801 --> 00:00:51.927
Yeah, it's really long

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:54.137
but what did you just turn on with it?

00:00:54.221 --> 00:00:57.224
Oh, that's just the What-If machine
I invented.

00:00:57.307 --> 00:00:59.268
You pose it a "what if" question

00:00:59.351 --> 00:01:02.980
and it generates a video
simulation of what would happen.

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:05.482
- Does it really work?
- Of course it works.

00:01:06.024 --> 00:01:07.693
It's just not very long.

00:01:07.776 --> 00:01:09.987
Ooh, ooh! I want to axe it a question.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:12.573
As a robot living among humans

00:01:12.656 --> 00:01:16.285
I've never really felt accepted at parties
or nude beaches.

00:01:16.368 --> 00:01:19.329
So, I've always secretly wondered...

00:01:19.454 --> 00:01:23.083
What if I was 500 feet tall?

00:01:23.166 --> 00:01:25.169
Let's watch, shall we?

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:40.559
My work here is done.

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:08.587
I'm so lonely since I came to the future.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:10.047
Will you be my friend?

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:11.507
Ow!

00:02:17.095 --> 00:02:18.680
Ohh!

00:02:20.474 --> 00:02:21.892
Who are you?

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:25.437
I'm a big robot and I want a big cereal.

00:02:25.521 --> 00:02:28.857
You, too? Will you be my friend?

00:02:29.483 --> 00:02:31.485
Put her there, pal.

00:02:32.236 --> 00:02:33.570
I meant your wallet.

00:02:33.654 --> 00:02:35.197
Three, two, one, zero.

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:29.209
Yeah, that calms the shakes.

00:03:29.293 --> 00:03:30.460
Hey!

00:03:34.965 --> 00:03:36.884
Okay, okay, come on now.

00:03:36.967 --> 00:03:39.178
Stop! The robot's not your enemy.

00:03:39.261 --> 00:03:40.971
He's just a poor, misunderstood...

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:00.157
Well, there goes the neighborhood.

00:04:01.408 --> 00:04:02.784
There goes another neighborhood.

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:03.952
We're jerked.

00:04:04.036 --> 00:04:06.246
Nothing can stop a monster that big.

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:08.957
Nothing except an even
equally big monster.

00:04:09.041 --> 00:04:13.128
This is a chance to try out
my experimental enlarging ray,

00:04:13.212 --> 00:04:15.172
but we'll need a guinea pig.

00:04:20.677 --> 00:04:21.970
What's this?

00:04:22.054 --> 00:04:24.056
Two meals in one week?

00:04:27.392 --> 00:04:28.769
- Got you!
- Sucker!

00:04:28.852 --> 00:04:31.104
Friends, help! A guinea pig tricked me.

00:04:34.733 --> 00:04:35.984
What?

00:04:38.654 --> 00:04:42.032
So, now Zoidberg is big, huh?

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:43.909
That's more like it.

00:04:43.992 --> 00:04:47.371
Who's intimidating who now, big city?

00:04:47.454 --> 00:04:50.290
Hello, Mr. Chase Manhattan Bank.

00:04:50.374 --> 00:04:53.544
Deny my credit card application, will you?

00:04:56.713 --> 00:04:59.508
Ah, the famed Apollo Theater.

00:04:59.591 --> 00:05:02.386
Boo me off stage on open-mike night?

00:05:02.469 --> 00:05:04.263
I'll show you.

00:05:07.099 --> 00:05:09.184
Hey, I called this city.

00:05:09.268 --> 00:05:11.144
Quit touching my stuff.

00:05:11.228 --> 00:05:12.771
Tell it to the claw.

00:05:12.855 --> 00:05:15.774
Bite my colossal metal ass.

00:05:52.436 --> 00:05:54.938
Who wants lobster bisque?

00:06:01.653 --> 00:06:02.779
- Hey, Bender.
- Huh?

00:06:02.863 --> 00:06:04.156
Want to make Shrinky Dinks?

00:06:12.581 --> 00:06:15.751
Who put this in here?

00:06:21.715 --> 00:06:24.343
No!

00:06:27.846 --> 00:06:29.473
Are you people satisfied?

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:32.100
This gentle visitor is dying

00:06:33.268 --> 00:06:35.562
and we'll never even know why he came.

00:06:35.646 --> 00:06:37.314
I'll... Tell you...

00:06:37.397 --> 00:06:39.942
with my final breath.

00:06:42.486 --> 00:06:46.281
I came here with a simple dream...

00:06:46.365 --> 00:06:50.536
A dream of killing all humans

00:06:50.619 --> 00:06:53.330
and this is how it must end?

00:06:54.706 --> 00:07:00.170
Who's the real
seven-billion-ton robot monster here?

00:07:00.879 --> 00:07:03.006
Not... I.

00:07:05.092 --> 00:07:07.427
Not... I.

00:07:12.099 --> 00:07:14.226
Good night, sweet prince.

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:19.273
Interesting stuff.

00:07:19.356 --> 00:07:21.400
Stay tuned for more:

00:07:28.073 --> 00:07:29.241
Well, Leela,

00:07:29.324 --> 00:07:31.451
care to give the what-if machine a whirl?

00:07:31.535 --> 00:07:32.786
Maybe later.

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:35.163
I mean, I don't know what to ask about.

00:07:35.247 --> 00:07:37.165
Come on, woman, just pick something.

00:07:37.249 --> 00:07:40.043
Yeah, be more impulsive, like this.

00:07:42.379 --> 00:07:44.339
Go, man, go.

00:07:45.591 --> 00:07:48.594
I can be really impulsive.
It just takes me awhile.

00:07:52.139 --> 00:07:54.391
All right, Professor, let's do it.

00:07:54.474 --> 00:07:56.310
Make that machine
show me what would happen

00:07:56.393 --> 00:07:58.020
if I was a little more impulsive.

00:07:58.145 --> 00:07:59.396
Just a little.

00:08:01.064 --> 00:08:02.107
Not too much.

00:08:04.067 --> 00:08:07.696
Hey, guys, look what I bought
on a wild impulse...

00:08:07.779 --> 00:08:08.989
New boots.

00:08:09.072 --> 00:08:13.243
They're like my old ones
but with a crazy green stripe. Whoo!

00:08:13.327 --> 00:08:15.078
Never know what I'm going to do next.

00:08:19.208 --> 00:08:21.668
Leela, could you come
in here for a moment?

00:08:21.752 --> 00:08:24.463
I have something important to tell you.

00:08:24.546 --> 00:08:27.174
I can't live forever and I need an heir...

00:08:27.257 --> 00:08:29.635
Someone to spend my vast riches

00:08:29.718 --> 00:08:33.222
and take care of my man-eating anteaters
when I'm gone.

00:08:35.807 --> 00:08:38.018
The others simply aren't
levelheaded enough.

00:08:38.143 --> 00:08:40.812
They're too impulsive... not like you.

00:08:40.896 --> 00:08:45.025
Not like old, predictable,
dull-as-dishwater Leela.

00:08:45.108 --> 00:08:47.194
Hello? New boots.

00:08:47.277 --> 00:08:49.821
That's why I've made you my sole heir.

00:08:49.905 --> 00:08:51.198
The day I die,

00:08:51.281 --> 00:08:53.867
you'll be a very wealthy woman.

00:08:53.951 --> 00:08:57.162
Oh, my, yes... Incredibly wealthy.

00:08:57.246 --> 00:08:59.122
The day I die...

00:08:59.206 --> 00:09:01.542
Because you're so un-impulsive.

00:09:02.292 --> 00:09:03.418
- Hi-ya!
- Oh!

00:09:07.881 --> 00:09:09.716
You've killed me!

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:11.260
You've killed me!

00:09:11.343 --> 00:09:13.053
Oh, God, what have I done?

00:09:13.136 --> 00:09:15.722
I just told you.
You've killed me!

00:09:19.935 --> 00:09:22.604
Okay, just try to be nonchalant.

00:09:25.649 --> 00:09:27.943
All right, so you're nonchalant.

00:09:28.026 --> 00:09:30.028
Quit rubbing our noses in it.

00:09:30.112 --> 00:09:32.656
Sweet giant anteater of Santa Anita!

00:09:32.739 --> 00:09:35.117
The professor's been eaten
by giant anteaters!

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:36.410
What?

00:09:36.493 --> 00:09:39.037
If you ask me, it's mighty suspicious.

00:09:39.121 --> 00:09:40.622
I'm going to call the police...

00:09:40.706 --> 00:09:42.249
Right after I flush some things.

00:09:42.332 --> 00:09:44.751
Police. Bah! Nosy meddlers.

00:09:44.835 --> 00:09:46.420
It so happens I have

00:09:46.503 --> 00:09:50.883
mail-order degrees
in Murderology and Murderonomy.

00:09:50.966 --> 00:09:52.926
Zoidberg is afoot.

00:09:53.010 --> 00:09:55.554
Perhaps the professor's
files can clear things up.

00:09:55.637 --> 00:09:58.265
Let's see, citation for public nudity,

00:09:58.348 --> 00:10:00.601
conspiracy to commit public nudity.

00:10:00.684 --> 00:10:03.228
Ah-ha! A new will naming...

00:10:04.646 --> 00:10:06.648
you as his sole heir!

00:10:06.732 --> 00:10:08.317
That doesn't prove I killed him.

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:10.694
It's a video will.
It shows you killing him.

00:10:15.824 --> 00:10:17.409
Hi-ya!

00:10:17.492 --> 00:10:21.496
All right, anteater number one,
who are you protecting?

00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:23.165
Is it anteater number two?

00:10:24.166 --> 00:10:26.168
Don't stick your tongue out at me.

00:10:26.251 --> 00:10:28.295
I need a name.

00:10:28.378 --> 00:10:30.547
What? How do you spell that?

00:10:31.507 --> 00:10:33.425
What are you hacking off?

00:10:33.509 --> 00:10:38.305
Is it my torso? It is! My precious torso!

00:10:38.388 --> 00:10:41.725
Hermes, quiet. I'm deducing things.

00:10:44.728 --> 00:10:46.396
What do you got? Disposal trouble?

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:47.814
No! Everything's just...

00:10:47.898 --> 00:10:49.566
Sure is shocking about the professor.

00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:51.401
And now Hermes is mysteriously missing.

00:10:51.527 --> 00:10:53.695
Anyhow, it doesn't affect me, Bender.

00:10:53.779 --> 00:10:55.405
Hey, what's this?

00:10:55.489 --> 00:10:57.658
Hermes' dreadlocks? And his arm?

00:10:57.741 --> 00:10:59.117
Leela, I'm shocked.

00:10:59.701 --> 00:11:03.747
Food goes in the disposal.
Hair and flesh go in the trash.

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:05.999
I'm sorry. I couldn't stop.

00:11:06.083 --> 00:11:07.084
Well, wait.

00:11:07.167 --> 00:11:09.002
Don't you care that I murdered Hermes?

00:11:09.086 --> 00:11:10.337
Not even a little.

00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:12.089
There's nothing wrong with murder

00:11:12.172 --> 00:11:14.383
just as long as you let
Bender wet his beak.

00:11:14.466 --> 00:11:15.759
You're blackmailing me?

00:11:15.843 --> 00:11:17.845
Blackmail is such an ugly word.

00:11:17.928 --> 00:11:19.137
I prefer extortion.

00:11:19.221 --> 00:11:21.181
The "X" makes it sound cool.

00:11:24.268 --> 00:11:25.561
Please, I'm made of metal.

00:11:25.644 --> 00:11:27.437
Like you're really going
to hurt me with...

00:11:27.521 --> 00:11:29.439
Hey, what are you doing
with that microwave?

00:11:38.615 --> 00:11:40.200
Okay, that's it.

00:11:40.284 --> 00:11:42.035
No more killing.

00:11:42.119 --> 00:11:44.037
Next time you feel like killing,

00:11:44.121 --> 00:11:45.747
just have a stick of gum.

00:11:45.831 --> 00:11:48.417
Now to dispose of the body.

00:11:49.459 --> 00:11:51.420
Honk, honk.

00:11:51.503 --> 00:11:54.798
Wow. Sporty go-cart, Leela.
So hip and sexy.

00:11:54.882 --> 00:11:56.133
Not like you at all.

00:11:57.301 --> 00:11:58.635
Do you have any gum?

00:11:58.719 --> 00:11:59.803
No.

00:12:12.713 --> 00:12:14.089
Ah! The gang's all here.

00:12:14.193 --> 00:12:15.402
Who are you?

00:12:15.485 --> 00:12:16.570
Scruffy, the janitor.

00:12:16.653 --> 00:12:18.155
I've never seen you before.

00:12:18.238 --> 00:12:20.157
I've never seen you before, neither.

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:21.408
Quiet, please.

00:12:21.491 --> 00:12:26.538
I've called you all here to the parlor
to watch as I gradually solve the crime.

00:12:26.622 --> 00:12:29.917
One of the people in this room
is a big murderer.

00:12:34.046 --> 00:12:37.257
You see, the killer left one fatal clue...

00:12:37.341 --> 00:12:39.927
This boot print on
the professor's lab coat.

00:12:40.010 --> 00:12:41.386
Couldn't be me.

00:12:41.470 --> 00:12:42.721
I never wear boots.

00:12:44.264 --> 00:12:45.265
See?

00:12:45.349 --> 00:12:47.601
Ew! What smells like boot feet?

00:12:47.684 --> 00:12:50.145
This is preposterous.

00:12:50.229 --> 00:12:51.813
Obviously, the murderer is...

00:12:56.693 --> 00:12:58.445
My next clue came at 4:15

00:12:58.529 --> 00:12:59.863
when the clock stopped

00:12:59.947 --> 00:13:02.366
and another came two hours later, at 4:15

00:13:02.741 --> 00:13:06.370
when I discovered the murdered body
of Amy's dead, deceased corpse.

00:13:09.373 --> 00:13:11.750
Scruffy knows who killed them people.

00:13:11.834 --> 00:13:14.086
In Scruffy's opinion, it were...

00:13:17.339 --> 00:13:19.633
So... It's just as I suspected all along.

00:13:19.716 --> 00:13:21.718
The crime is unsolvable.

00:13:30.102 --> 00:13:31.478
Huh?

00:13:31.562 --> 00:13:34.857
A letter from Bender, my good friend.

00:13:34.940 --> 00:13:36.650
"Dear Dr. Jerkberg,

00:13:36.733 --> 00:13:39.486
"if you're reading this, I'm already dead.

00:13:39.570 --> 00:13:42.990
"The person who killed me was... was..."

00:13:44.116 --> 00:13:46.451
My God. It can't be.

00:13:46.535 --> 00:13:47.911
The murderer. It was...

00:13:48.871 --> 00:13:50.455
I'm bored.

00:13:50.539 --> 00:13:51.790
You're boring, Zoidberg.

00:13:51.874 --> 00:13:53.208
I'm going to go watch TV.

00:13:53.292 --> 00:13:55.919
Could you get the lights on your way out?

00:13:58.255 --> 00:14:00.883
- Whatcha eating?
- Lobster.

00:14:00.966 --> 00:14:02.342
- You want some?
- Sure.

00:14:02.426 --> 00:14:06.305
You know, I think I finally figured out
what's behind all these mysterious deaths.

00:14:06.388 --> 00:14:07.514
Really?

00:14:07.598 --> 00:14:10.642
Was Planet Express built
on an Indian graveyard?

00:14:10.726 --> 00:14:11.935
- No.
- No?

00:14:12.019 --> 00:14:15.147
- No.
- Then... Then...

00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:16.648
It was you.

00:14:16.732 --> 00:14:18.108
I don't know what came over me.

00:14:18.192 --> 00:14:20.402
I killed one person on impulse.

00:14:20.485 --> 00:14:22.571
Then I had to kill another and another.

00:14:22.654 --> 00:14:24.615
Well, that covers
the first three killings.

00:14:24.698 --> 00:14:27.701
And now, to make sure you won't talk...

00:14:27.784 --> 00:14:32.706
I'm going to have to do
something really impulsive.

00:14:36.168 --> 00:14:37.252
So, Fry...

00:14:37.336 --> 00:14:39.963
What do you think of the impulsive new me?

00:14:40.047 --> 00:14:41.298
I like it.

00:14:41.381 --> 00:14:45.677
Good, now let me just get the lights.

00:14:49.306 --> 00:14:50.933
I really like it.

00:14:54.937 --> 00:14:57.856
Who else has a question
for the What-If machine?

00:14:57.940 --> 00:14:59.191
Scruffy? Fry?

00:14:59.274 --> 00:15:00.692
I have a question.

00:15:00.776 --> 00:15:02.528
What if Bender was really giant?

00:15:02.611 --> 00:15:04.279
You idiot, we already saw that.

00:15:04.363 --> 00:15:06.823
I know, I liked it.
I want to see it again.

00:15:06.907 --> 00:15:09.576
We're not seeing it again.
Ask something less stupid.

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:10.994
All right, how about this?

00:15:11.078 --> 00:15:13.121
What if I never fell
into that freezer doodle

00:15:13.205 --> 00:15:14.581
and came to the future jiggy?

00:15:14.665 --> 00:15:16.250
That question is less stupid,

00:15:16.333 --> 00:15:19.127
though you asked it in
a profoundly stupid way.

00:15:19.211 --> 00:15:23.215
What would happen if Fry
never came to the future?

00:15:33.851 --> 00:15:34.893
Hello!

00:15:34.977 --> 00:15:37.062
Pizza delivery for...

00:15:37.145 --> 00:15:38.730
I.C. Wiener?

00:15:38.814 --> 00:15:40.065
Oh, crud.

00:15:43.610 --> 00:15:46.363
Here's to another lousy millennium.

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:55.873
Ow!

00:15:57.124 --> 00:15:59.918
I should have left you
floating in the toilet. Oh!

00:16:04.923 --> 00:16:05.924
What is it?

00:16:06.008 --> 00:16:09.511
It appears that the very fabric
of space-time has ripped.

00:16:09.595 --> 00:16:11.388
Hey, look, an ugly, scared guy. Boo!

00:16:17.603 --> 00:16:18.812
Who are you monsters?

00:16:18.896 --> 00:16:20.314
Is one of you I.C. Wiener?

00:16:20.397 --> 00:16:23.275
If that's his pizza,
than I'm Icy whatever.

00:16:30.532 --> 00:16:33.160
You believe me about the monsters,
right, Mr. Panucci?

00:16:33.243 --> 00:16:35.329
There's only three real monsters, kid...

00:16:35.454 --> 00:16:37.915
Dracula, Blacula and Son of Kong.

00:16:37.998 --> 00:16:42.044
Now, quit picking your nose
and knead that dough.

00:16:44.671 --> 00:16:47.508
Hey, the usual, Professor Hawking?

00:16:47.591 --> 00:16:50.052
No, today I'd like something good.

00:16:50.135 --> 00:16:53.555
Hawking, you're all right.
I'll make you the usual.

00:16:53.639 --> 00:16:54.848
Hey, Stephen Hawking.

00:16:54.932 --> 00:16:57.559
Aren't you that physicist
that invented gravity?

00:16:57.643 --> 00:16:59.019
Sure, why not?

00:16:59.102 --> 00:17:00.562
Let me ask you something.

00:17:00.646 --> 00:17:03.315
Has anyone ever discovered
a hole in nothing with monsters in it?

00:17:04.608 --> 00:17:05.734
'Cause if I'm the first,

00:17:05.817 --> 00:17:07.861
I want them to call it a Fry hole.

00:17:07.945 --> 00:17:10.531
There is nothing to be concerned about.

00:17:10.614 --> 00:17:13.200
I must go. There is much to do.

00:17:16.119 --> 00:17:18.038
Hey, Hawking, your pizza's ready.

00:17:18.121 --> 00:17:20.290
Toss it in the garbage.

00:17:25.003 --> 00:17:26.880
There he is. Seize him.

00:17:26.964 --> 00:17:28.006
Who said that?

00:17:28.090 --> 00:17:29.758
Hey! Hey! Ow!

00:17:35.097 --> 00:17:36.139
Who are you people?

00:17:36.223 --> 00:17:37.683
I'm Al Gore, and these

00:17:37.766 --> 00:17:40.018
are my vice-presidential action rangers,

00:17:40.102 --> 00:17:42.062
a group of top nerds whose sole duty

00:17:42.145 --> 00:17:45.399
is to prevent disruptions
in the space-time continuum.

00:17:45.482 --> 00:17:48.819
I thought your sole duty was to cast
the tie-breaking vote in the senate.

00:17:48.902 --> 00:17:51.697
That, and protect
the space-time continuum.

00:17:51.780 --> 00:17:53.073
Read the constitution.

00:17:53.156 --> 00:17:55.909
Hmm. So I guess
you'll want to see my Fry hole.

00:17:55.993 --> 00:17:58.996
Very much so, but first,
meet the action rangers.

00:17:59.079 --> 00:18:01.123
You already know Stephen Hawking.

00:18:01.206 --> 00:18:03.000
Also with us are Nichelle Nichols,

00:18:03.083 --> 00:18:04.585
A.K.A. Commander Uhura.

00:18:04.668 --> 00:18:08.213
Incoming transmission
from MCI One-Rate department.

00:18:08.297 --> 00:18:10.215
It sounds like a limited-time offer.

00:18:10.299 --> 00:18:11.884
Tell them I'm in the tub.

00:18:11.967 --> 00:18:14.595
To my left, you'll recognize Gary Gygax,

00:18:14.678 --> 00:18:16.221
inventor of Dungeons &amp; Dragons.

00:18:16.305 --> 00:18:20.142
Greetings. It's a... pleasure to meet you.

00:18:20.225 --> 00:18:22.436
And our summer intern, Deep Blue.

00:18:22.519 --> 00:18:25.522
The world's foremost
chess-playing computer.

00:18:25.606 --> 00:18:26.940
Bishop to knight four.

00:18:27.024 --> 00:18:30.110
Not all missions can
be solved with chess, Deep Blue.

00:18:30.194 --> 00:18:31.904
Someday you'll understand that.

00:18:31.987 --> 00:18:33.280
Where am I, anyway?

00:18:33.363 --> 00:18:37.117
You're traveling in a specially equipped
terrestrial transport module.

00:18:37.201 --> 00:18:38.202
A school bus.

00:18:40.287 --> 00:18:41.580
So what do you nerds want?

00:18:41.663 --> 00:18:44.458
It's about that rip
in space-time that you saw.

00:18:44.541 --> 00:18:46.502
I call it a Hawking hole.

00:18:46.585 --> 00:18:48.462
No fair. I saw it first.

00:18:48.545 --> 00:18:52.090
Who is The Journal of Quantum Physics
going to believe?

00:18:52.174 --> 00:18:55.344
Mr. Fry, the time disruption
indicates that some event

00:18:55.427 --> 00:18:59.473
was supposed to happen,
but didn't due to a quantum fluctuation.

00:18:59.556 --> 00:19:02.351
That's why we had to beat you
with tennis rackets.

00:19:02.434 --> 00:19:05.062
If we don't go back there
and make the event happen

00:19:05.187 --> 00:19:08.148
the entire universe will be destroyed

00:19:09.107 --> 00:19:11.985
and as an environmentalist,
I'm against that.

00:19:17.824 --> 00:19:19.076
So then my chair tilted back

00:19:19.159 --> 00:19:21.245
and I almost fell
into this freezer thingy.

00:19:21.328 --> 00:19:23.372
I call it a Hawking chamber.

00:19:23.455 --> 00:19:25.332
But instead of falling in
and getting frozen,

00:19:25.415 --> 00:19:26.708
I missed and wanged my head.

00:19:26.792 --> 00:19:28.752
Well, it's obvious
what should have happened.

00:19:28.836 --> 00:19:30.796
That wang to the head
should have killed you.

00:19:30.879 --> 00:19:31.922
What?

00:19:32.005 --> 00:19:33.632
Let's finish the job.

00:19:33.715 --> 00:19:36.009
No, wait! There must be a peaceful...

00:19:37.177 --> 00:19:39.054
- Hold him down.
- Check.

00:19:41.598 --> 00:19:43.016
Ow!

00:19:48.564 --> 00:19:52.109
Something's wrong. Murder isn't working
and that's all we're good at.

00:19:52.192 --> 00:19:55.571
Let's try something else.
Maybe we should...

00:19:55.654 --> 00:19:58.323
Put the dice away before I take them away.

00:19:58.407 --> 00:20:00.284
Wait, I'm getting an idea.

00:20:00.367 --> 00:20:02.703
What if Fry was supposed to get frozen?

00:20:02.786 --> 00:20:03.829
Yes.

00:20:03.912 --> 00:20:06.623
Shove him in the tube.
It was my idea.

00:20:08.333 --> 00:20:11.670
Hey, there he is again
and he brought nerds.

00:20:11.753 --> 00:20:14.006
Take this!

00:20:14.089 --> 00:20:15.299
Get in the tube, dummy.

00:20:15.382 --> 00:20:18.510
We only have a few seconds
before the universe is destroyed.

00:20:21.054 --> 00:20:22.556
All right, but I need a weapon

00:20:22.639 --> 00:20:24.850
to fight off drunken robots
when I wake up.

00:20:24.933 --> 00:20:27.311
Here, take my plus-one mace.

00:20:28.478 --> 00:20:30.856
Okay, here I go.

00:20:33.984 --> 00:20:36.236
You fool! You foolish fool!

00:20:36.320 --> 00:20:38.697
Eh. What's the worst thing
that can happen?

00:20:56.173 --> 00:20:57.341
Great.

00:20:57.424 --> 00:20:59.843
The entire universe was destroyed.

00:20:59.927 --> 00:21:02.262
Destroyed? Then where are we now?

00:21:02.346 --> 00:21:07.100
I don't know, but I can darn well tell you
where we're not... the universe.

00:21:07.184 --> 00:21:09.561
Eternity with nerds.

00:21:09.645 --> 00:21:13.148
It's the Pasadena Star Trek
convention all over again.

00:21:13.232 --> 00:21:16.860
Anyone want to play Dungeons &amp; Dragons
for the next quadrillion years?

00:21:16.944 --> 00:21:18.070
- Yes, please.
- Sure.

00:21:18.153 --> 00:21:19.279
Pawn to rook eight.

00:21:19.363 --> 00:21:20.948
I'm a tenth-level vice president.

00:21:23.033 --> 00:21:24.910
That story was preposterous.

00:21:24.993 --> 00:21:27.037
Stephen Hawking in a pizzeria.

00:21:27.120 --> 00:21:29.998
This thing isn't worth
the gold it's made of.

00:21:31.166 --> 00:21:34.962
Anyway, "The Thing Longer"
seems to be a rousing success.

00:21:35.045 --> 00:21:36.338
Good work.

00:21:36.421 --> 00:21:38.006
Right on, Professor.

00:21:40.425 --> 00:21:45.013
So that's what things would be like
if I'd invented the Finlonger.

00:21:46.431 --> 00:21:48.392
A man can dream, though.

00:21:49.017 --> 00:21:51.895
A man can dream.